# What EAS Build uploads.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. When .easignore exists, eas-cli uses it *instead
# of* .gitignore -- not in addition to it. So this file has to restate the
# exclusions that matter, and it silently stops tracking .gitignore the moment
# the two drift. Keep them in step.
#
# The whole reason it exists: .gitignore carries `*.db`, because the 134 MB
# corpus DB is generated and must never be committed. Under .gitignore alone,
# EAS would exclude it from the archive and the build would *succeed* -- and
# ship an app with no database, failing only on the device, on first open. The
# negation at the bottom is the point of this file. Everything above it is
# there so the negation can exist without dragging up node_modules with it.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
.pnpm-store/
.next/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Native projects: `expo prebuild` regenerates these on the build machine.
android/
ios/
.expo/

# Signing material must never leave this machine -- EAS holds the keystore.
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Secrets.
#
# Deliberately the broad glob, not the three specific names this used to list:
# .env.production, .env.development and .env.test matched none of them, and
# because this file REPLACES .gitignore, anything unmatched here is uploaded.
# Add a negation only for a file that is known non-secret and needed by the
# build -- and only after reading it.
.env*

# Python (packages/scraper plays no part in a mobile build)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Scrape artefacts and snapshots
data-snapshots/
.snapshots/
raw-scrape/
*checkpoint*.json
*.stale.bak

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Databases -- generated artefacts, same rule as .gitignore...
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# ...except the bundled corpus, which IS the app's content. Sidecars stay
# excluded: SQLite recreates -wal/-shm on the device, and the committed -wal
# here is 0 bytes anyway.
!apps/mobile/assets/db/quran.db
